n the right I have M the person's  mass times a the acceleration of the  elevator and therefore the person notice  that when the elevator is accelerating  the normal force and the gravitational  force do not have the same magnitude  that is they don't cancel out so now I  can solve for FN and I can find that  it's just M times the quantity a plus G  have you ever noticed that at the bottom  of an elevator ride when you're  accelerating upward you feel heavier and  at the top when you're decelerating you  often feel lighter you can see that if I  change a to minus a in this example that  I'll get the normal force is equal to M  times G minus a and this explains that  feeling of lightness it's always good to  check that your answers match physical  intuition and I encourage you to go and  play with elevators and other physical  phenomena around you while you're going  through this course to see if your  answers make physical sense
 

